---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NavBar from '../components/NavBar.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Coding Standards" description="amber coding standards, how we write code">
  <NavBar />
  <main>
    <h1>Coding Standards</h1>

    <section class="section">
      <p>
        amber is C++17. Four-space indentation, no tabs, 100-column soft limit. The
        <code>.clang-format</code> file is the source of truth, run it on any code you touch.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider-thick" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>General</h2>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>C++17.</strong> No C++20 features yet. Stay portable.</li>
        <li><strong>clang-format.</strong> Run <code>clang-format -i &lt;files&gt;</code> on code you touch.</li>
        <li><strong>No tabs.</strong> Four-space indentation only.</li>
        <li><strong>100-column soft limit.</strong> Wrap long lines, but don't break early.</li>
        <li><strong>No comments that restate the code.</strong> If the code is clear, don't comment it.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>File Organization</h2>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>lib/</strong> + <strong>include/agent/</strong>, the UI-free core. No UI concerns here.</li>
        <li><strong>tui/</strong>, the ncurses client. Depends on the library through <code>AgentHooks</code>, never the reverse.</li>
        <li><strong>bench/</strong>, the KPI harness. Same layering rules.</li>
        <li><strong>tools/</strong>, tool implementations (read, write, search, bash).</li>
        <li><strong>prompts/</strong>, system/tool prompts in Markdown, loaded at runtime.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Naming Conventions</h2>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>snake_case</strong> for variables, functions, and files.</li>
        <li><strong>PascalCase</strong> for classes and types.</li>
        <li><strong>UPPER_SNAKE_CASE</strong> for macros and constants.</li>
        <li><strong>_suffix</strong> for private member variables.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>SPDX Headers</h2>
      <p>Every new source file must carry the SPDX header:</p>
      <div class="terminal">
        <pre>// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// Copyright 2026 Jacek Trefon (www.trefon.com)</pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Commit Messages</h2>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>Imperative mood.</strong> "fix drawer scroll" not "fixed drawer scroll".</li>
        <li><strong>Scoped prefixes.</strong> <code>tui: fix drawer scroll</code>, <code>bench: add scenario</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Tests for behavior changes</strong> go in <code>tests/run_tests.cpp</code>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Linting</h2>
      <p>Both must come back clean before a commit:</p>
      <div class="terminal">
        <pre>make lint     # run clang-tidy over project sources
make analyze  # run cppcheck as a second opinion</pre>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
